      "headline": "Info Edge Q2 billings up 12.8%, shares fall 3%",
      "essay": "Info Edge reported standalone billings of ₹822.3 crore for Q2 FY27, up 12.8% from ₹729 crore a year earlier. For H1 FY27, billings rose 13.5% to ₹1,559.3 crore. The stock still slipped 3% after the update.\n\nThe recruitment segment, which includes Naukri, grew 12.6% to ₹613.8 crore. Management said underlying growth was 14% to 15% once renewal timing differences are stripped out. That gap matters: renewal timing can flatter or depress reported growth from quarter to quarter. In Q1 FY27, recruitment billings grew 17.5% on a reported basis, but underlying growth was also around 15%.\n\nFor someone holding Info Edge, the read is that the core recruitment engine is growing in the mid-teens, not the 30%+ that pure-play SaaS firms report. The market is focused on that gap and on the Shiksha drag, not the headline beat.",
