  "view": "Gold is caught between two forces. Lower Treasury yields and central bank buying support prices, but hawkish Fed talk and high oil-driven inflation keep the dollar firm. The metal has bounced from $4,066 to above $4,200, yet it remains range-bound. Without a clear break, the near-term direction is unclear.",
