      "headline": "Info Edge Q2 billings up 12.8%, recruitment grows 12.6%",
      "essay": "Info Edge reported standalone billings of INR 8.22 billion (USD 63.4 million) for the second quarter ended 30 September 2026, up 12.8% from INR 7.29 billion a year earlier. Recruitment solutions, the core Naukri business, grew 12.6% to INR 6.14 billion. That was slower than the 14.4% growth in the first quarter.\n\nThe company said the recruitment performance was affected by one-off deferrals in renewals. Kotak Institutional Equities maintained its expectation of 14-15% billings growth for FY2027, compared with 14.9% growth in the first half. 99acres, the real estate vertical, grew 21.2% to INR 1.48 billion, and Jeevansathi rose 18.4% to INR 397 million. Shiksha fell 27.2% to INR 205 million.\n\nFor the six months ended 30 September, revenue rose 13.5% to INR 15.59 billion. The update is subject to review by the audit committee and auditors. For a holder, the key point is that the recruitment slowdown looks temporary, and the smaller verticals are growing faster than the core.",
