  "stance": "neutral",
  "view": "Naukri's September index rose 2% year-on-year to 3,053, with AI/ML roles up 20% and Auto up 11%. But IT/Software Services fell 4% and metros like Delhi-NCR and Mumbai dropped 6% each. The job market is steady but selective, so no clear direction for Infoedge today.",
  "stories": [
    {
      "headline": "Naukri JobSpeak rises 2% as AI/ML hiring grows 20%",
      "essay": "White-collar hiring grew 2 per cent year-on-year in September, with the Naukri JobSpeak Index reaching 3,053 from 3,002 a year earlier. AI/ML roles rose 20 per cent, the fastest-growing category, while Auto grew 11 per cent. BPO/ITES and GCC hiring each added 4 per cent.\n\nHiring fell in IT/Software Services, Pharma/Biotech and FMCG, each down 4 per cent, and Healthcare slipped 3 per cent. Hospitality and Travel dropped 11 per cent and Education 18 per cent. By experience, fresher hiring rose 1 per cent, the 4-7 years band fell 2 per cent, and demand for 8-12 years, 13-16 years and over 16 years rose 5 per cent, 7 per cent and 5 per cent respectively.\n\nHyderabad led metros with 9 per cent growth, followed by Chennai at 6 per cent and Bengaluru and Kolkata at 4 per cent each. Pune was stable, while Delhi-NCR and Mumbai each declined 6 per cent. For Infoedge, the index shows steady but selective demand, with growth concentrated in specialised AI skills and experienced professionals rather than broad-based hiring.",
      "sources": [1]
    }
  ]
