      "headline": "Jio Platforms sets terms for India's largest-ever IPO",
      "essay": "Jio Platforms is targeting a valuation of $106 billion in an IPO that would be India's largest ever. The price band is Rs 1,065 to Rs 1,119 per share, raising up to Rs 30,213 crore through 27 crore fresh shares, with no offer for sale by existing shareholders. Anchor bidding opens October 19, public subscription runs October 21 to 23.\n\nThe issue would dethrone Hyundai Motor India, which raised Rs 27,858.75 crore in October 2024. Jio's last grey market premium was Rs 172 as of October 10, implying a listing price near Rs 1,291, a 15.4% premium. The fresh issue means the money goes to the company, not to exiting investors.\n\nJio is one of a dozen companies tapping the primary market in October, after 96 IPOs raised over Rs 1.1 lakh crore so far in 2026. JM Financial's Neha Agarwal said appetite for quality paper remains structural, supported by domestic liquidity, though she flagged that investor behaviour is shifting from momentum to valuation discipline. For anyone holding Jio, the pricing and demand for the largest Indian listing in history is the number that matters this week.",
